                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "**Dying Light**\n\nDying Light is one of those zombie games that manages to make simple movement feel incredibly satisfying. The parkour system is easily the highlight of the game. Running across rooftops, jumping between buildings and escaping hordes of infected makes Harran feel like a playground where every street and rooftop can become an escape route.\n\nThe day and night cycle is another great addition. During the day, you can explore, loot and complete missions relatively safely, but once night falls, everything changes. The atmosphere becomes much more tense, and suddenly running through the city feels like a matter of survival.\n\nThe melee combat is brutal and satisfying, especially when you start upgrading your weapons and skills. There is something incredibly fun about modifying a weapon and then testing it on a group of zombies. The RPG progression also gives you a constant reason to explore and improve your character.\n\nThe story isn't anything revolutionary, and some missions can become repetitive, with plenty of fetch quests and predictable moments. The characters and writing are also not always as strong as the gameplay. But fortunately, the core gameplay is good enough to carry the experience.\n\nDying Light really shines when you're simply free-roaming the city, parkouring across rooftops, looking for supplies and trying to survive whatever happens next. It also has a great co-op experience, making the chaos even more enjoyable with friends.\n\n**Pros:**\n+ Excellent parkour system  \n+ Great day/night cycle  \n+ Brutal and satisfying melee combat  \n+ Huge open world to explore  \n+ Lots of weapons, upgrades and activities  \n+ Very fun co-op  \n\n**Cons:**\n- Story can be predictable  \n- Some missions become repetitive  \n- A few frustrating mission designs  \n- Some technical issues  \n\nOverall, Dying Light is a fantastic open-world zombie game. It isn't perfect, but the combination of parkour, melee combat, exploration and survival creates an experience that is extremely difficult to put down.\n\n**8.5/10 — Highly Recommended.**",
